## Context

- Phase 1a (#1005) done: SWI/SNF classifier — 157 ARID1A-mut, 72 SMARCA4-mut, 16 dual, 1874 WT across 2119 lines.
- Phase 1b (#1006) done: Metabolic dependency screen — 1590 KEGG metabolic genes screened. SMARCA4-ovarian has strong OXPHOS signal.
- Phase 2 (#1007) done: Cross-atlas validation — 104 convergent metabolic genes (SL in both ARID1A & SMARCA4). 34 are OXPHOS/ETC genes. HMGCR does NOT cross-validate (ARID1A-specific). SMARCA4 mito genes (MICOS13, HIGD2A, COX6C) DO cross-validate to ARID1A.
- Phase 3 (#1008) done: Pathway enrichment — OXPHOS is dominant (4.3x enriched, FDR=2.56e-13). Lipoic acid also enriched (5.6x, FDR=4.45e-03). Ranked analysis confirms SMARCA4 OXPHOS shift (median d=-0.905).
- Phase 4 (#15) done: TCGA expression analysis across 6 cohorts (LUAD, LUSC, UCEC, OV, STAD, COAD). 77/104 (74%) convergent genes show significant differential expression (FDR<0.05) in at least one cohort — PASSES 50% criterion. UCEC (42 sig, 216 ARID1A-mut) and STAD (49 sig, 102 ARID1A-mut) drive results. OV skipped (only 2 SWI/SNF-mut patients). 26/34 OXPHOS genes significant (mean log2FC=+0.16 upregulated). Direction: 84 up, 25 down in mutant.
- Phase 5 done: Drug sensitivity (PRISM), summary visualizations (#16).
- Task #16 done: 3 summary figures generated (OXPHOS heatmap, cross-validation forest, drug sensitivity dot plot) in output/cancer/swisnf-metabolic-convergence/figures/.
- Key finding: SWI/SNF metabolic convergence is OXPHOS-driven, not cholesterol. OXPHOS genes are upregulated in SWI/SNF-mutant tumors across multiple tissue types, supporting compensatory OXPHOS dependence as a targetable vulnerability.
- Drug angle: metformin/IACS-010759/phenformin as primary candidates (not statins).
- Slim extraction approach (download_expanded_tcga.py) enabled 4 new cohorts within 8GB RAM / 13GB disk constraints.
- Code: src/cancer/swisnf_metabolic_convergence/ (01-07 scripts + download_expanded_tcga.py)
- Results: data/results/swisnf-metabolic-convergence/phase1a/, phase1b/, phase2/, phase3/, phase4/, phase5/
- Remaining task: #14 (evaluate Phase 1-5 results, pending, p4)
